<title>EGYPT: Egyptian pound interbank rates fall.</title>
<headline>Egyptian pound interbank rates fall.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound fell on Thursday to 9-3/4 and 10 percent from Wednesday's 10-1/16 and 10-1/4 percent in a private sector market that was, as usual, liquid at end-week, bankers said.</p>
<p>One-week rates also fell, to a range of 10 and 10-1/4 percent from 10-1/8 and 10-3/8 percent, the bankers added.</p>
<p>State-owned banks kept their minimum interbank lending rate at 10-1/2 percent, they said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
